hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27582","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umm Mubashshir, wife of Zayd ibn Harithah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in Hafsah's house and said: None who witnessed Badr and Hudaybiyah will enter Hell. Hafsah said: Does not Allah, Exalted and Glorious, say: There is none of you except coming to it? She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be quiet, then We will save those who feared."
"27583","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from Umm Mubashshir, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever plants a plant or sows a crop, and a man, beast, animal, or bird eats from it, it is charity for him."
"27584","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umm Mubashshir, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me while I was in a garden of the gardens of Banu al-Najjar containing graves of theirs who died in Jahiliyyah. He heard them being punished, and went out saying: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, are they indeed punished in their graves? He said: Yes, a punishment heard by beasts."
"27585","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umm Mubashshir, she said: The slave boy of Hatib came and said: By Allah, Hatib will not enter Paradise. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You lie; he witnessed Badr and Hudaybiyah."
